# One Facebook page per line: <page URL> [webhook URL] [interval=<duration> | at="<cron expr>"]
# - webhook URL is optional — omit it to use DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL from .env.
#   Use $VAR_NAME (defined in .env) instead of a literal URL here — this file
#   is meant to be safe to commit/share, .env is not.
# - interval is optional — how often to poll (e.g. 15m, 6h, 1d). Defaults to 1d.
# - at is optional — poll at exact time(s) instead, standard 5-field cron
#   syntax (minute hour day month weekday), e.g. at="0 7 * * *" = daily at 7am.
#   Use interval= OR at=, not both.
# Either way, this only works if the script itself runs at least that often
# (or every minute, for at=) — see the crontab entry.
# Lines starting with # are ignored.
#
# Example: https://www.facebook.com/SomePage webhook=$SOMEPAGE_WEBHOOK_URL at="0 7 * * *"
